= Pattern Cluster Boundaries <sec:pattern-clusters>

// Case A: target positive for H-ING, H-PROMO, H-ATTR, H-SCOPE, H-OUTLOOK.
== Case A
Industry reports describe the framework as groundbreaking. Accuracy improved in
@tab:main, highlighting its transformative effect from representation learning to clinical
deployment. Despite these challenges, the approach opens exciting new avenues.

// Case B: target positive for H-PRED.
== Case B
@tab:main serves as a presentation of the ablation results.

// Case C: target positive for H-TERM.
== Case C
The proposed encoder compresses the input. This feature extractor then feeds the representation
module, and the latent processor is optimized jointly. No alternate term is defined.

// Case D: evidence-supported analytical tail and evaluation.
== Case D
Accuracy increased by 4.2 percentage points under the noisy test condition, highlighting the
measured improvement reported in @tab:main and the preregistered analysis @smith2024.

// Case E: resolvable attribution.
== Case E
Smith et al. @smith2024 report that the effect holds for Dataset-A under the stated noise model;
they do not claim that it generalizes beyond that setting.

// Case F: exact three-item scope.
== Case F
The evaluation measures accuracy, latency, and peak memory; @tab:main reports all three metrics for
every baseline.

// Case G: precise predication and explicitly defined terminology.
== Case G
The latent variable $z$ represents the posterior mean. We define the encoder as the feature
extractor and the decoder as the reconstruction module; these terms retain those meanings below.

// Case H: honest limitation and concrete future test.
== Case H
The evaluation is limited to Dataset-A, so the cross-domain effect may not generalize. Future work
will test Dataset-B with the same preregistered metrics and noise model.
